  "integrated_statement": "Geographic isolation is associated with a recurrent global floral and reproductive island-syndrome direction and independently with increasing experimental pollen limitation. The plant response contains partially separable reproductive-assurance and floral-accessibility pathways. Post-hoc functional triangulation shows the clearest current-pollen-limitation compatibility for autonomous selfing, with additional global architecture concordance. Taxonomic structure determines how the response is represented across flora layers but does not identify its cause.",
